# The embedded LibGlass-1.0, LibShowcase-1.0 and LibAccountSync-1.0: the packager fetches them
# (.pkgmeta externals) and Tools/deploy.ps1 copies them from checkouts. Never
# committed. The other libraries under Libs/ ARE vendored and tracked.
Libs/LibGlass-1.0/
Libs/LibShowcase-1.0/
Libs/LibAccountSync-1.0/

# Packaged zips. Release artifacts belong in GitHub Releases (the packager
# attaches them to the tag) and on CurseForge — never committed.
dist/

# Probe / SavedVariables captures pulled off the client. These carry real
# character names, GUIDs and realm data, and this repo is public.
*.sv.lua
AltStableProbeDB*.lua
docs/captures/

# The CurseForge description, kept locally: its images are CurseForge's own
# uploads (media.forgecdn.net), so it differs from README.md and is pasted by hand.
README.curseforge.md

# Local scratch
*.log
*.zip
settings.ini

# Agent/editor local state. Skills are shared project tooling and belong in the
# repo (AltTracker tracks the same file); settings.local.json stays local.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .NET build output, if any tooling lands here later
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# Generated cutouts - regenerate from screenshots, never commit
Tools/RenderCutout/out/

# Scene SOURCE artwork: the PNG masters the TGAs were exported from, and the
# owner's reference screenshots. 110 MB that the addon never loads and that git
# would carry forever - binary files do not shrink out of history later.
# PROMPTS.md records how every scene was generated, and README.md the exact
# ImageMagick line that turns a master into a texture, so this is reproducible
# rather than lost. The committed .tga files are what the client reads.
Media/Scene/*.png
Media/Scene/References/

# Recipe generator page cache (Wowhead HTML) - regenerable, never committed
Tools/RecipeData/.cache/
